          "type": "concept",
          "title": "BMI: A 190-Year-Old Population Tool",
          "content": "**Body mass index (BMI)** is weight in kilograms divided by height in meters squared. It was devised in the 1830s by Belgian mathematician **Adolphe Quetelet** to describe the 'average man' across populations -- not to diagnose individuals.\n\nStandard adult cutoffs:\n• **Under 18.5** -- underweight\n• **18.5-24.9** -- 'normal'\n• **25-29.9** -- overweight\n• **30+** -- obesity\n\n**What BMI does well:** it is free, fast, and at the population level it tracks risk of type 2 diabetes, heart disease, and early death reasonably well.\n\n**What it misses:**\n• It cannot tell **muscle from fat** -- muscular athletes often score 'overweight'\n• It ignores **where fat sits** (belly vs hips)\n• Cutoffs don't fit everyone -- the WHO suggests **lower action points for many Asian populations**, who develop diabetes risk at lower BMIs\n• It shifts with age as muscle declines\n\nThink of BMI as a **screening flag**, not a verdict.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">BMI IN ONE PICTURE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Weight (kg) / height (m) squared</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"220\" height=\"120\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Under 18.5</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Underweight</text><rect x=\"320\" y=\"180\" width=\"220\" height=\"120\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">18.5 - 24.9</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Normal</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"180\" width=\"220\" height=\"120\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"670\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">25 - 29.9</text><text x=\"670\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Overweight</text><rect x=\"800\" y=\"180\" width=\"220\" height=\"120\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"910\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">30 and up</text><text x=\"910\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Obesity</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"400\" width=\"800\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">BLIND SPOTS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Muscle vs fat -- fat location -- ethnicity -- age</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"560\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Useful for populations, rough for individuals</text></svg>",
            "caption": "BMI categories and what they cannot see"
          }
