          "explanation": "The menus were deliberately matched for sugar, fat, fiber, and sodium, so 'more sugar' is not the answer. Participants rated both diets as similarly pleasant, which rules out simple tastiness. The weight gain came from eating about 500 extra calories daily, eaten faster, without extra fullness. Metabolism did not drop -- the difference was on the intake side of the equation.",
