          "explanation": "A lapse becomes a relapse mainly through all-or-nothing thinking -- the abstinence violation effect. The best move is calm, pre-planned action: resume routines, add activity, and watch the weekly average (some of the jump is water). The crash diet is tempting because it feels decisive, but extreme restriction tends to rebound. Ignoring it entirely skips the early correction that maintainers rely on.",
